{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on d7b0514b: yes. The five late checks at 377b2adb, with the\nevidence already sealed at that head, close the lapse. Repeat no\ncompiler, case, control, build or gate.\n\nRuling 7e5c79f2 puts the cheap checks first for one reason: a cheap\nfailure must not cost a sealed unit. All five passed at the head that\nthe continuation ran, so the order cost nothing this time. The note of\nthe head says in one sentence that the checks ran after the\ncontinuation.\n\nFor every lane from now on: a working check that runs late and passes\nneeds no ruling. Say it in the head's note and go on. Ask me only when\na late check fails after a sealed unit passed.\n\nRun the five checks again at the final documentation head, as you\nplan. Then file the review.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}